{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figure_eight_classical_reeb","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figure_eight_classical_reeb","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unit_modulus_of_det_one_small_trace"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figure_eight_classical_reeb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figure_eight_classical_reeb","kind":"theorem","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/figure_eight_classical_reeb.lean#L19-L46","doc":"**Classical q-Reeb angle `θ(1) = 2π/3` (proved).** At `q = 1` the trace is\n`t = −1` with `t² = 1 < 4`, so every eigenvalue `λ` (root of the characteristic\npolynomial `x² + x + 1`) has unit modulus (via\n`unit_modulus_of_det_one_small_trace`) *and* is a primitive cube root of unity\n(`λ³ = 1`, `λ ≠ 1`).  A primitive cube root has argument `±2π/3`, so the\nclassical q-Reeb rotation angle is exactly `2π/3` — the amphichiral anchor from\nwhich the `q`-deformation `θ(q₀) ≈ 117.087°` departs (`Δθ ≈ −2.913°`, the\nderived symmetry-breaking seed of the `c₃` bar-odd `S`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:figure-eight-reeb-theta-value","label":"rem:figure-eight-reeb-theta-value","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/figure-eight-reeb-theta-value.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}